---
import LegalDocument from '@/components/LegalDocument.astro';
import { href } from '@/lib/href';
import { ISSUES_URL, NAME } from '@/lib/site';
---

<LegalDocument
  title={`Privacy — ${NAME}`}
  description={`How ${NAME} and this website handle your data: in short, they don't collect any.`}
  updated="12 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    <strong>In short: neither the {NAME} app nor this website collects personal data.</strong> There
    is no account, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking and no cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <p>
    {NAME} works on your computer. The archives you open, the files you compress and the passwords
    you type are handled locally by the app and the 7-Zip installed on your computer, and are never
    sent anywhere.
  </p>
  <p>The app makes network requests in exactly two situations:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Checking for updates.</strong> When automatic update checks are on (the default), the
      app downloads <code>updates/latest.json</code> from this website when it starts and every few
      hours while it runs. The request carries no identifier beyond what any HTTPS request reveals
      (your IP address and the app’s user agent). Turn it off in Settings → Updates.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Installing an update</strong>, when you choose to: the app downloads the installer for
      your platform from this website (or from GitHub Releases if the website is unavailable).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Settings and the list of recent archives are stored in a settings file on your computer
    (<a href={href('/docs/reference/settings/')}>where it lives</a>). Uninstalling the app does not
    remove it; delete it to remove every trace.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website is a static site hosted by GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics.
    The theme you pick is remembered in your browser’s local storage and never leaves it. GitHub,
    as the host, receives the technical data of each request (such as your IP address) to serve and
    protect the site; see the{' '}
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>
  <p>Fonts are served from this site itself; no third-party font or script services are used.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Open an issue on <a href={ISSUES_URL}>GitHub</a>.</p>
</LegalDocument>
